9.	Upgrading/Reloading Motoring Expenses

	There is no need to lose any data when upgrading or reloading 
Motoring Expenses. If you cannot start Motoring Expenses after re-loading
or upgrading Motoring Expenses carry out the following routine:

1. Go to the $:\system\apps\motoring directory and delete the preferences
file (if it exists). 
2. Go to the $:\motoring directory 
3. Cut the files in this directory (identified with registration numbers) 
4. Paste these files into the $:\motoring\backup folder. 
5. Open Motoring Expenses 
6. Enter the vehicle's registration as requested by the application. 
7. Go to the $:\motoring\backup directory 
8. Cut or Copy the files previously pasted into here and paste them into
the $:\motoring directory (overwrite the empty databases created when the
new vehicle was entered) 
9. Your data should now be restored, re-register your program with your
existing registration code (if registered) and you will now have a fully
functional Motoring Expenses. 

where $=drive letter c or d
